{"id": "en_flash_flood_p2", "total": 69.23, "segments": [{"text": "Part two. Mark stands on high ground with a dead phone in dark rain.", "start": 0.0, "end": 4.4}, {"text": "Flood water hides dangerous deep holes, washed-out roads, and debris beneath the surface.", "start": 5.02, "end": 9.16}, {"text": "He stays on higher ground because walking into dark water risks getting swept away.", "start": 9.72, "end": 13.46}, {"text": "One. Mark uses his bright flashlight to signal toward the distant highway overpass.", "start": 13.15, "end": 18.18}, {"text": "He flashes the light 3 times continuously to signal distress into the dark sky.", "start": 18.68, "end": 21.98}, {"text": "Two. Mark keeps a safe distance from the edge on the high rocky hill.", "start": 21.770000000000003, "end": 25.98}, {"text": "Remember that 6 inches of moving water can knock an adult off their feet.", "start": 25.98, "end": 29.34}, {"text": "Down below, 12 inches of fast water carries his sedan into the deep river.", "start": 29.74, "end": 33.64}, {"text": "Flood water hides hidden hazards so stepping into the current is a deadly mistake.", "start": 34.28, "end": 37.86}, {"text": "Three. Mark waves his arms high when rescue lights appear on the road above.", "start": 37.47, "end": 42.04}, {"text": "Emergency responders spot his signal light and park on safe dry upper ground.", "start": 42.58, "end": 46.46}, {"text": "A rescue worker calls out to Mark to confirm he is completely safe.", "start": 46.96, "end": 49.6}, {"text": "Mark walks carefully toward the team while staying far away from rushing water.", "start": 50.28, "end": 53.38}, {"text": "The emergency crew gives him warm blankets inside their rescue vehicle high above.", "start": 53.88, "end": 56.8}, {"text": "Staying on high ground saved Mark from the violent flash flood on highway 4.", "start": 57.52, "end": 60.92}, {"text": "Turn Around, Don't Drown; never drive into flooded roads. Follow for a new scenario tomorrow.", "start": 61.52, 